    "result_text": "All 10 tests pass, including the three new `Cp04Tests`. The build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the optional owner `email` field per the spec: present-and-valid \u2192 stored/returned lower-cased; present-and-invalid \u2192 400; absent \u2192 accepted.\n\nChanges made, following the existing `telephone` precedent:\n\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `email` property to the `OwnerFields` schema, which propagates to the generated `OwnerFieldsDto` (request) and `OwnerDto` (response, via `allOf`).\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `email` column, getter/setter, and `toString` entry. MapStruct auto-maps the same-named property in both directions, so `OwnerMapper` needed no changes.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `normalizeEmail` helper: blank/absent \u2192 `null`; otherwise validate against a syntactic email pattern (throwing `InvalidEmailException` on failure) and lower-case. Wired into both `addOwner` and `updateOwner`.\n- **`InvalidEmailException.java`** (new) + **`ExceptionControllerAdvice.java`** \u2014 a 400 handler mirroring the telephone error format.\n- **DB schemas** \u2014 added the `email` column to all four `schema.sql` files (hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres). The seed `data.sql` files for hsqldb and mysql used positional `INSERT INTO owners VALUES (...)`, which broke once the column count changed, so I gave those inserts explicit column lists (h2/postgres already used explicit columns).\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 10, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
